(3928923, 553946, 3569, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by dfstevenson:</b></div><hr/><i> DNMC </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Missing link is a biological term for evolution missing links between pre-historic and modern animals/man.  So my vulture ate the missing link animals, thus no link has been found.  Must have went over many DPCers heads or no sense of humour this challenge?  :)<br/> <br/>P.S. thanks for the comments!!!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-07-23 14:27:36.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by dfstevenson: DNMC   Missing link is a biological term for evolution missing links between pre-historic and modern animals/man.  So my vulture ate the missing link animals, thus no link has been found.  Must have went over many DPCers heads or no sense of humour this challenge?  :) P.S. thanks for the comments!!!', '2007-07-23 15:26:15.000000', '2007-07-23 15:27:36.000000', 0),
