(3944212, 555104, 80878, '<td valign="top">***From the Critique Club***<br/>As A Christian I agree with you! <br/> <br/>First Impression - the most important one: <br/>  Nice, I like it. I love the idea of finding the missing link to the chain, and I think you''ve done it probably the best.<br/>Composition: <br/>  I think there probably is a more appealing lay out for the tools, but I like how the link really looks like it has just been uncovered rather then just resting on the dirt. <br/>Subject:<br/>  I think you could add a little umph, to the picture by placing more emphases on the link; perhaps using lighting.<br/>Technical (Colour, focus, and light):<br/>  I like the rustic feel, again maybe emphasize the link with some more lighting, but the colours are great. The POV, and DOF are also right on.<br/>Artistic:<br/>  Very creative, well laid out.<br/>To grow its vote?:<br/>  I think the picture is great, but for higher votes it needs a bit more of what I call the wow factor, you know that thing that makes you want to look at a picture for a long time. I''m not sure how you''d go about doing that with this picture.<br/>Summary:<br/>  Good picture, creative, well laid out. Definitely has room for improvement.<br/> <br/>Woa, Personal best! Keep that trend up! I also really like city of lights<br/> <br/>Happy shooting, CBoydrun!<br/></td>', '***From the Critique Club***As A Christian I agree with you!  First Impression - the most important one:   Nice, I like it. I love the idea of finding the missing link to the chain, and I think you''ve done it probably the best.Composition:   I think there probably is a more appealing lay out for the tools, but I like how the link really looks like it has just been uncovered rather then just resting on the dirt. Subject:  I think you could add a little umph, to the picture by placing more emphases on the link; perhaps using lighting.Technical (Colour, focus, and light):  I like the rustic feel, again maybe emphasize the link with some more lighting, but the colours are great. The POV, and DOF are also right on.Artistic:  Very creative, well laid out.To grow its vote?:  I think the picture is great, but for higher votes it needs a bit more of what I call the wow factor, you know that thing that makes you want to look at a picture for a long time. I''m not sure how you''d go about doing that with this picture.Summary:  Good picture, creative, well laid out. Definitely has room for improvement. Woa, Personal best! Keep that trend up! I also really like city of lights Happy shooting, CBoydrun!', '2007-07-28 01:27:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(3944231, 555520, 80878, '<td valign="top">***From the Critique Club***<br/> <br/>First Impression - the most important one:<br/>  WOW! Very cool lightening! but how does it apply to this challenge?<br/>Composition:<br/>  I like the wood in the corner; it balances the picture, and gives your eye a choice, the lightening or the wood. I do find however that the image is a bit grainy (probably a result of High ISO as its a night shot hard to avoid, especially with all that haze and/or fog!) I think I would have liked to see a much longer shutter to try and lighten up the background a bit, to try and bring some colour into it.<br/>Subject:<br/>  Fascinating on sooo many levels. There is just something about lightening that makes us as people want to stare... Thus making it a great subject for pictures. this one seems to do a cool dance about the sky also! lol<br/>Technical (Colour, focus, and light): <br/>  I guess this is where the grainy thoughts and the trying to lighten the background should have been written. However all that aside the lightening showed up great!<br/>Artistic:<br/>  I think the redeeming factor artistically, is the wood in the corner, otherwise it falls a little short in the artistic side. (Personally speaking of course) but All the same its a picture I would have liked to have taken!<br/>To grow its vote?:<br/>  I think the thing that hurt your votes the most is people struggling to see how this fits into the challenge. I like the picture but in good conscious I couldn''t vote it very high in this challenge, as I don''t feel it really applies!<br/>Summary:<br/>  Great picture, very cool, you must have been very excited after taking it. However I think your title is a bit of a mad grab to get this picture to fit inside the competition. There are also some lighting adjustments to try and keep in mind next big storm. As hard as it can be try not to max out the ISO, and use a very long shutter, then post process the sky a bit darker. Anyways Glad I got to see this one!<br/> <br/>Hey this image is above your average good, job! I also really like world of purity and Black cats<br/> <br/>Happy shooting, CBoydrun.<br/></td>', '***From the Critique Club*** First Impression - the most important one:  WOW! Very cool lightening! but how does it apply to this challenge?Composition:  I like the wood in the corner; it balances the picture, and gives your eye a choice, the lightening or the wood. I do find however that the image is a bit grainy (probably a result of High ISO as its a night shot hard to avoid, especially with all that haze and/or fog!) I think I would have liked to see a much longer shutter to try and lighten up the background a bit, to try and bring some colour into it.Subject:  Fascinating on sooo many levels. There is just something about lightening that makes us as people want to stare... Thus making it a great subject for pictures. this one seems to do a cool dance about the sky also! lolTechnical (Colour, focus, and light):   I guess this is where the grainy thoughts and the trying to lighten the background should have been written. However all that aside the lightening showed up great!Artistic:  I think the redeeming factor artistically, is the wood in the corner, otherwise it falls a little short in the artistic side. (Personally speaking of course) but All the same its a picture I would have liked to have taken!To grow its vote?:  I think the thing that hurt your votes the most is people struggling to see how this fits into the challenge. I like the picture but in good conscious I couldn''t vote it very high in this challenge, as I don''t feel it really applies!Summary:  Great picture, very cool, you must have been very excited after taking it. However I think your title is a bit of a mad grab to get this picture to fit inside the competition. There are also some lighting adjustments to try and keep in mind next big storm. As hard as it can be try not to max out the ISO, and use a very long shutter, then post process the sky a bit darker. Anyways Glad I got to see this one! Hey this image is above your average good, job! I also really like world of purity and Black cats Happy shooting, CBoydrun.', '2007-07-28 01:47:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3944355, 552788, 66515, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Excellent shot. Not a lot to really remark on to improve it. Playing with clouds, as suggested in one comment, might have improved the look of the clouds but I don''t think it would discernibly change the overall impact of the picture. <br/> <br/>Judging from some of the comments it would seem some believed the link to the challenge was a bit weak. I disagree myself but I can see where they are coming from. I think the biggest difference between your image and the shot that got third is the third place shot bopped the voter over the head with its relation to the challenge. Your shot, photographically, I would say is at least on par with it. At least in my opinion anyways...</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Excellent shot. Not a lot to really remark on to improve it. Playing with clouds, as suggested in one comment, might have improved the look of the clouds but I don''t think it would discernibly change the overall impact of the picture.  Judging from some of the comments it would seem some believed the link to the challenge was a bit weak. I disagree myself but I can see where they are coming from. I think the biggest difference between your image and the shot that got third is the third place shot bopped the voter over the head with its relation to the challenge. Your shot, photographically, I would say is at least on par with it. At least in my opinion anyways...', '2007-07-28 03:56:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3944359, 553792, 66515, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club! <br/> <br/>Great idea for this challenge. Without your description I would have sworn this was a shot of old train tracks. <br/> <br/>Previous comments spoke about the contrast and the noise. I actually like it this way. The high contrast and noise gives its an old feeling and really helps to establish a mood. <br/> <br/>Composition? I imagine that there is water just outside the frame of your shot so your options were likely limited if you wanted to keep it out of the shot. Again, I like it the way it is.<br/> <br/>Overall? Really excellent entry. Keep up the good work.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Great idea for this challenge. Without your description I would have sworn this was a shot of old train tracks.  Previous comments spoke about the contrast and the noise. I actually like it this way. The high contrast and noise gives its an old feeling and really helps to establish a mood.  Composition? I imagine that there is water just outside the frame of your shot so your options were likely limited if you wanted to keep it out of the shot. Again, I like it the way it is. Overall? Really excellent entry. Keep up the good work.', '2007-07-28 04:01:58.000000', NULL, 0),
